    <!-- Guide & Disclaimer Dialog -->
    <string name="guide_title">ℹ️ Guide &amp; Disclaimer</string>
    <string name="guide_close">Close</string>
    <string name="guide_body">📖 About MMT7821-Client\nMMT7821-Client is an independent, open-source DIY Android client for the Medtronic Guardian Connect (MMT-7821) transmitter and Enlite / Guardian Sensor 3 electrodes. It operates 100%% offline without CareLink servers or device whitelisting.\n\n🚀 Quick Start &amp; Pairing Guide\n1. Charger Reset: Disconnect the transmitter from the sensor and place it on the charger for at least 10 seconds until the green LED flashes, then remove it.\n2. Pairing: Open Settings, tap \'Scan for Transmitter (BLE)\' or enter the MAC address, and tap \'Connect\'. Wait ~10–15 seconds for cryptographic pairing to complete.\n3. Sensor Start &amp; Warm-up: Attach the transmitter to the sensor on your body. The 2-hour hardware warm-up will start automatically.\n4. Calibration: Once warm-up finishes (\'Waiting for Calibration\'), enter a fingerstick blood glucose reading from your meter. Calibrate every 6–12 hours when glucose is stable.\n\n⏳ Sensor Lifespan &amp; Restart\nGuardian Connect MMT-7821 enforces the 6-day sensor lifespan in transmitter hardware. To restart a sensor session, physically detach the transmitter from the sensor, place it on the charger for 15–20 minutes to reset the internal session timer, and reattach it to begin a new 2-hour warm-up.\n\n⚠️ Medical &amp; Legal Disclaimer (IMPORTANT)\nFOR RESEARCH AND EDUCATIONAL (DIY) PURPOSES ONLY. MMT7821-Client is NOT an approved medical device and has not been evaluated by the FDA or any regulatory authority. Software or Bluetooth failures may occur. NEVER make insulin dosing or treatment decisions based solely on this app—always confirm with a certified blood glucose meter. By using this software, you assume full responsibility and all associated risks.</string>

